{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:stable-certified-padding",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(\\delta_n=2^{-p_n-1}\\), let \\(\\mathcal B_n\\) be the coordinate box of radius \\(\\delta_n\\) about \\((\\widetilde X,\\widetilde R,\\widetilde C)\\) on \\(\\kappa_n=0\\), and suppose the public controls are exact dyadic inputs.  Put\n\\[\n\\mathcal H_n=n+T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\alpha^{-1}+p_n+q_n+1.\n\\]\nThere are finite constants \\(K_\\star,k_\\star\\), depending only on \\(c,C_0,B,\\sigma,r_0\\), such that for all sufficiently large \\(n>r_0\\), if every coordinate of \\(\\mathcal B_n\\) is at most \\(T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+1\\) in absolute value, then\n\\[\n0\\le\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\n\\le K_\\star\\mathcal H_n^{k_\\star}.\n\\]\nIf in addition every donor matrix \\(X'\\in\\mathcal B_n\\) satisfies\n\\[\ns_r(X')\\ge3cn/4,\\qquad s_{r+1}(X')\\le cn/4,\n\\qquad s_1(X')\\le3C_0n/2,\n\\]\nthen\n\\[\n\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\n\\le K_\\star\\mathcal H_n^{k_\\star}\n\\bigl(2^{-p_n}+2^{1-q_n}\\bigr).\n\\]\nEvery nonnegative radius recorded as a summand of either \\(\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}\\) or \\(\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\\) obeys the corresponding upper bound.",
    "depends_on": [
      "def:spectral-gate",
      "def:analytic-halfwidth",
      "def:donor-allowance",
      "def:analytic-interval",
      "def:observation-encoding",
      "def:directed-rounding-model",
      "def:certified-handle",
      "def:numerical-padding",
      "lem:certified-error-recurrence"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(T=T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+1\\).  On \\(\\kappa_n=0\\), every coordinate of every\npoint of \\(\\mathcal B_n\\) has absolute value at most \\(T\\).  At a feasible\non-gate point, the gate and the rank-\\(r\\) truncation give\n\\[\n\\|X_r^+\\|_{\n\\mathrm{op}}\\le {2\\over cn},\n\\qquad\n\\|Z_{p,n}\\|_2,\\|Z_{q,n}\\|_2\\le {\\sqrt nT\\over\\sigma}.               \\tag{1}\n\\]\nSince \\(h_n=\\|D_n\\|_{\n\\mathrm{op}}\\) and\n\\(s_{Z,n}\\le h_n(\\|Z_{p,n}\\|_2^2+\\|Z_{q,n}\\|_2^2)^{1/2}\\),\n\\[\nt_{Z,n}\\le {\\sqrt{2n}T\\over\\sigma}.                                 \\tag{2}\n\\]\nFurthermore \\(0<\\beta_\\alpha(t)\\le\\alpha/4\\), and hence\n\\[\n0<\\zeta_\\alpha(t)\\le \\Phi^{-1}(1-3\\alpha/8).                        \\tag{3}\n\\]\nEquations (1)--(3), the definitions of \\(R_{0,n},t_{-,n},t_{+,n},W_n\\), and\n\\(C_{r,\\alpha}\\le C(1+\\log(1/\\alpha))\\) show that \\(W_n\\) is bounded by a\nfixed polynomial in\n\\(\\mathcal H_n=n+T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\alpha^{-1}+p_n+q_n+1\\).\nAlso\n\\[\n|\\widehat\\theta_n|=|RX_r^+C|\\le {2T^2\\over c},                       \\tag{4}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nd_n\\le K_0\\sigma^2\\ell_n n^{-2}\n\\left({\\sqrt nT\\over\\sigma}+\\sqrt{\\ell_n}\\right)^2.                 \\tag{5}\n\\]\nThus every feasible on-gate endpoint is bounded by\n\\(K\\mathcal H_n^k\\), while the off-gate interval has fixed radius\n\\(M_0=B^2/c\\).  The handle can always return the outward hull of these branches.\nThis proves\n\\[\n0\\le\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\n\\le K\\mathcal H_n^k.                                                  \\tag{6}\n\\]\nExact-dyadic public controls contribute zero input radius.\n\nNow impose the three stable spectral inequalities in the statement.  Relative\nto \\(\\tau=(cn/2)^2\\), every retained or discarded squared singular value is\nseparated from the cutoff by at least\n\\[\n\\min\\{(3cn/4)^2-(cn/2)^2,(cn/2)^2-(cn/4)^2\\}\n=\\frac{3c^2n^2}{16}.                                                   \\tag{7}\n\\]\nThe certified-error recurrence lemma therefore applies to the sharp projector,\npseudoinverse, scalar-calibration, and endpoint graph.  If its precision test\nsucceeds, it gives\n\\[\n\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\n\\le K\\mathcal H_n^k(2^{-p_n}+2^{1-q_n}).                              \\tag{8}\n\\]\nIf that test fails, its failure implies\n\\(1\\le K\\mathcal H_n^d(2^{-p_n}+2^{1-q_n})\\).  Multiplying (6) by this\ninequality and increasing the fixed exponent proves (8) in that case as well.\nEvery recorded summand is nonnegative and is at most the displayed sum, so it\nobeys the same applicable bound.  This proves the lemma.",
    "justification": "The stable-box lemma converts the recurrence into a uniform observable padding bound and retains a valid coarse-hull case at inadequate precision.",
    "gap": "The bound includes input and working precision in its polynomial majorant and applies summand by summand.",
    "consumer": "The statistical transfer can integrate numerical padding rather than relying on a high-probability backward-error slogan.",
